The first implementation is in place as a standalone Python executable with no dependencies. It parses the declared type/signature layer before analyzing bodies, which matters for forward calls and for distinguishing a genuine argument mismatch from an unknown expression.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The implementation treats closed booleans/enums as finite sets and integers as inclusive interval unions. That is enough to prove cases such as `(false, false, false/true)` exhaustiveness and `x > 5 and x < 3` unsatisfiability without relying on line numbers or diagnostic text.
