The second run now matches all single-diagnostic cases except two false `switch_inexhaustive` reports caused by coverage bookkeeping after a wildcard, plus the tuple coverage case. The real diagnostics are otherwise separated correctly: `c07` is only `rebinding`, `c09` only `arg_not_accepted`, and `c12` combines its return-type error with `vacuous_arm` as the specification implies.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
A wildcard over an integer domain is “all intervals,” while a wildcard over a finite tuple domain is a concrete finite set. The bookkeeping must preserve those representations when they follow an opaque guarded arm; otherwise an already exhaustive switch can look incomplete merely because an earlier arm was not provable.
